explain how neurons, synapses and receptors process information and approach behavior on the proximate level, covering reflexes, key stimuli, conditioning and learning. Addiction, stress and hormones are included, with attention to how behavior research is designed.","verificationStatus":"primary-source-confirmed"}'),
