lication, protein synthesis, epigenetic regulation, telomeres, cancer genes, CRISPR/Cas9 and other gene technology tools, and DNA fingerprinting. They compare genetic and environmental variation for biodiversity and evolution and evaluate uses of human genetics.","verificationStatus":"primary-source-confirmed"}'),
