ling and sustainability.","verificationStatus":"primary-source-confirmed"}'),
  ('a677fff9-6447-51fa-b167-7bcca3285731', 'saxony-anhalt-curriculum-repository', 'DE-ST', 'openlpm-starter-draft', 'DE-ST-LP-INF-sjg11-12-kurs4-aktuelle-entwicklungen-gesellschaft', 'Sachsen-Anhalt Gymnasium Informatik Lehrplan, grades 11 to 12: Current developments in computing in their social context', '{"id":"DE-ST-LP-INF-sjg11-12-kurs4-aktuelle-entwicklungen-gesellschaft","label":"Sachsen-Anhalt Gymnasium Informatik Lehrplan, grades 11 to 12: Current developments in computing in their social context","labelDe":"Aktuelle Entwicklungen der Informatik im gesellschaftlichen Kontext","sourceUrl":"https://www.bildung-lsa.de/files/b45de329c361a40a2f0a7211902d5815/FLP_Informatik_Gym_01082022_swd.pdf","provenance":{"date":"2026-10-28","added_by":"claude-session","extracted_by":"llm","review_status":"author-draft","contributor_notes":"Read from https://www.bildung-lsa.de/files/b45de329c361a40a2f0a7211902d5815/FLP_Informatik_Gym_01082022_swd.pdf (30-31). Lehrplan: Fachlehrplan Gymnasium Informatik, 01.08.2022 (In Kraft seit 2017, Anpassung 2022). Not reviewed by a person. Topics are chosen from one or more Themenfelder; AI appears as one of several listed examples and as one possible project."},"jurisdiction":"DE-ST","issuingBody":"Ministerium für Bildung des Landes Sachsen-Anhalt (published via the Landesportal / LISA and the Bildungsserver Sachsen-Anhalt)","mandateType":"curriculum-unit","schoolType":"Gymnasium","subject":"informatik","unitNumber":"Kurs 4","gradeFrom":11,"gradeTo":12,"topicTags":["media_society","ai_ml"],"lehrplanEdition":"01.08.2022 (In Kraft seit 2017, Anpassung 2022)","adoptionDate":"2022-08-01","dateGranularity":"day","statementText":"Students examine current developments in computing and their effects on society and the environment, choosing topics such as artificial intelligence, social networks, virtual worlds or resource use of devices. They assess chances, risks and sustainability, and may build or train a small AI system.","description":"Students examine current developments in computing and their effects on society and the environment, choosing topics such as artificial intelligence, social networks, virtual worlds or resource use of devices. They assess chances, risks and sustainability, and may build or train a small AI system.","verificationStatus":"primary-source-confirmed"}'),
